{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"debug":1},true],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"zotero":1,"inscriptions":7,"isBulletin":173},{"title":2,"author":3,"date":4,"citation":5,"uri":6},"Catania antica","Holm","1925","\u003Cspan>A. Holm, \u003Ci>Catania antica\u003C/i>, trad. da G Libertini (Catania: Libreria Tirelli di F. Guaitolini, 1925)\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/7VWTI6D2",[8],{"file":9,"uri":9,"title":10,"status":11,"editions":13,"editionAuthor":27,"type":28,"objectType":32,"material":36,"condition":51,"layoutDesc":52,"handNote":59,"date":85,"places":89,"geo":99,"country":94,"provenance":91,"provenanceGeo":103,"region":106,"settlement":96,"repository":107,"idno":111,"textLang":114,"tmNumber":15,"facsimile":118,"letterHeights":125,"publications":134,"zotero":144,"keywords":154,"html":165,"bibl":166,"bulletinDateSort":172,"citedRangeSort":167,"languageSort":115,"materialSort":37,"typeSort":29},"ISic000298","Dedication to the Genius of the city of Catania",{"_":12},"edited",[14,17,20,22,25],{"_":15,"type":16},"175826","TM",{"_":18,"type":19},"074187","EDR",{"type":21},"EDH",{"_":23,"type":24},"21900333","EDCS",{"type":26},"PHI",null,{"_":29,"ana":30,"ref":31},"dedication","#function.dedication","https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Dedication",{"_":33,"ana":34,"ref":35},"plaque","#object.plaque","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259",{"_":37,"ana":38,"type":39,"subtype":40,"resp":42,"ref":43,"placeName":44},"\n                                        Fine to medium-grained, banded, white, smelly marble, likely Proconnesian. Digital microscopy: heteroblastic fabric (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy)\n                                    ","#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Proconnesian","stone.marble",[41],"Proconnesian","#Coccato","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html",{"type":45,"ref":46,"location":49},"provenance",{"_":47,"target":48},"Marmara District","https://www.geonames.org/741729/marmara-adasi.html",{"geo":50},"40.61972,27.61694","",{"layout":53},{"p":54,"rs":55,"damage":51},"The text is preserved intact, over seven lines, although the edge\n                                        of the surviving stone clips the tops of the letters of the first line. The\n                                        letters diminish in size over the first four lines, with a vacat in the second\n                                        half of line four; the final three lines are larger again. The left margin of\n                                        the text is maintained regularly, the right margin varies from line to line.",{"_":56,"ana":57,"ref":58},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":60,"dimensions":61},"The letters are deeply but somewhat irregularly cut, with some\n                                    internal variation (e.g. A appears with both broken and straight bar; E appears both\n                                    as a tall narrow standard E and as a vertical stroke with a single horizontal bar\n                                    across the middle; V appears both as V and as Y). Interpuncts are mostly absent,\n                                    except after VC and CONS in the final two lines.",[62,70,76,83],{"type":63,"l":64,"from":65,"to":65,"h":66,"unit":67,"atLeast":68,"atMost":69},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","60-80","mm","60","80",{"type":63,"l":71,"from":72,"to":73,"h":74,"unit":67,"atLeast":75,"atMost":68},"Line 2-4","line2","line4","40-60","40",{"type":63,"l":77,"from":78,"to":79,"h":80,"unit":67,"atLeast":81,"atMost":82},"Line 5-7","line5","line7","50-70","50","70",{"type":84,"from":65,"to":72,"unit":67},"interlinear",{"_":86,"notBefore":87,"notAfter":88},"Munatidius is not otherwise known; the mention of three Domini\n                                    requires one of the periods 337—340, 367—378, 379—383, 388—395, 402—408, and 421. A\n                                    precise choice is not possible, but the consensus amongst scholars is for a date in\n                                    the 4th century rather than later.",337,421,[90,95],{"_":91,"type":92,"ref":93,"region":94},"Catina","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462270","Sicilia",{"_":96,"type":97,"ref":98,"region":94},"Catania","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2525068",[100],[101,102],37.49223,15.07041,[104,105],37.502748,15.083639,"Sicily",{"_":108,"role":109,"ref":110},"Museo Civico di Catania","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/018",{"_":112,"type":113},"2","inventory",{"_":115,"mainLang":116,"languages":117},"Latin","la",[115],{"n":119,"url":120,"height":121,"width":122,"desc":123,"surfaceType":124},"screen","ISic000298_tiled.tif","4192px","3680px","Photograph of front face by J. Prag","front",[126,129,131],{"atLeast":127,"atMost":128},60,80,{"atLeast":130,"atMost":127},40,{"atLeast":132,"atMost":133},50,70,[135,136,137,138,139,140,141,142,143],"Mommsen, 1883, CIL","L'année épigraphique: revue des publications épigraphiques relatives a l'antiquité romaine., 1888-","Korhonen, 2004, IMusCatania","Dessau, 1892-1916, ILS","Holm, 1925, Catania antica","Manganaro, 1958-1959, Iscrizioni latine e greche di Catania tardo-imperiale","Manganaro, 1988, La Sicilia da Sesto Pompeo a Diocleziano","Wilson, 1990, Sicily under the Roman Empire: the archaeology of a Roman province, 36 B.C. - A.D. 535","Manganaro, 1993, Greco nei pagi e latino nelle città della Sicilia romana tra I e VI sec. d.C.",[145,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153],"GQN8UZSI","R46KDTZX","2EUC82DH","XHMS9K6S","7VWTI6D2","BVD8KVF7","RZSFKACR","VF9MMBI9","JBI7CI5R",[155,156,157,29,33,158,159,160,161,162,160,163,164,116],"isic000298","dedication to the genius of the city of catania",{"_":12},"fine to medium-grained, banded, white, smelly marble, likely proconnesian. digital microscopy: heteroblastic fabric (identification based on pxrf, digital 